  "icon": "Landmark",
  "estMinutes": 13,
  "title": "Certify the interim payment and invoice the authority",
  "desc": "Register the contract and its guarantees, measure the period against the bill, recover the advance payment and hold retention, get the Engineer to issue the interim payment certificate and invoice the authority against it under the procurement law's payment window.",
  "longDesc": "On a government works contract the interim payment certificate is the document everything else hangs from. The advance payment is recovered through it, the retention is held on it, and the invoice that follows is only as good as the certificate behind it. The failure this arc is built to prevent is quiet and expensive: an invoice submitted against a certificate the Engineer has not issued sits in the authority's queue looking exactly like an invoice that is being processed, and the payment window everybody is relying on has not started at all. Certificate first, invoice second, with both dates recorded, is what makes a late payment a question with an answer.",
